Z||000011||84Bill||11-30-2001||08:48 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Monkeyman:<BR><B>  I'll be on it for a few minutes then nothing will work and I'll end up with a blank (white) screen.  At that point, not even Ctrl-Alt-Del will work.  <BR>HELP!!!!!!!!!!!!!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>No MM you dont have a virus<BR>Open the computer up and reseat all the cards and memory modules. I that does not work you may have toasted the motherboard and or Processor.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Formula88||11-30-2001||09:02 AM||||Don't bother with password protection on Windows 9x,ME.  It's useless.  All someone has to do is turn off the PC, turn it back on and log in as a different user.  They can then look at anything you've got.  Same is true for NT, if you use a FAT partition.  You can just boot to a floppy and read anything on the HDD.  You have to use NT/2000 and NTFS for it to have any real security.||||reg||13
